<h4 class="byline">'still in the dark ages'</h4>

<p>

<a href="http://www.nytimes.com/2007/11/09/nyregion/09sentence.html?_r=1&oref=slogin">Michael Brick</a>: With his long legs stretched out to cross at the ankles, his gaze like a vacant lot, Allan Cameron was sentenced yesterday to life in prison with no chance of parole for murdering a police officer during a midnight car chase through the streets of Flatbush.<br />
<br />
Mr. Cameron, 29, protested his fate.<br />
<br />
&#8220;The only thing I&#8217;m guilty of today, Your Honor,&#8221; he told the judge just before the sentence was handed down, &#8220;is being young, black and poor.&#8221;
